  "prefLabel": "Hum 317.05 Procedural Effect of Reconsideration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Hum 317.05 Procedural Effect of Reconsideration. Reconsideration initiated by the commission or on motion granted by the commission chair or presiding officer shall:\n\n(a) Stay the original order issued by the commission; and\n\n(b) Be completed with the issuance of a final decision no later than 45 days of the following, as applicable:\n\n(1) The issuance of the notice required by Hum 317.01(a); or\n\n(2) The granting of a motion for reconsideration and review.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Hum 300) #8815-A, eff 2-3-07",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/hum100-300.html"
}
